cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this repository — code, analysis or figures — please cite it as below.
  Roles and the evidence behind each one are in AUTHORS.md.
title: >-
  Adaptive Functional Network Reconfiguration for Predicting Individual
  Working-Memory Performance (The Gammas, Neuromatch Academy CompNeuro 2026)
abstract: >-
  Does functional-connectivity reconfiguration between low (0-back) and high (2-back)
  working-memory load predict individual performance in unseen participants? HCP N-back
  data, 336 analytic participants, 360 Glasser ROIs summarised into a 78-feature
  connectivity fingerprint over 12 Cole-Anticevic networks, cross-validated ridge
  regression against a permutation null. Results, protocols and limitations:
  docs/final-report.md.
